@AJenbo hey, thanks for reaching out. Analysis engine, a PHP parser, if you will in this LSP, which is now growing to largely replace Intelephense. The reason I have all my own things is because Intelephense doesn't go far enough, PHPActor doesn't go far enough in actually analyzing the code for my needs.

That being the case, my thinking is that perhaps we might conflict as well. And maybe that's what you're getting at, is trying to write out a configuration so that we don't provide duplicate information to the user. I would be happy to see what you have in mind. Maybe you can outline your thoughts in this ticket and submit a PR with what you think would be a good solution?

Inspector Lestrade, hold off on analyzing for now until we get things cleared up as to the direction we want to go.
